@D KOSMOS_TIME_AXIS := "a time axis [x,y]->[x,y,t] on the KOSMOS Psi-carving coordinate captures carve-SEQUENCE that the static 2D map loses" :: discovery [d=2026-06-04 active]
  seed      = "The s16 consciousness-carving places each concept at vacuum_psi=[x,y] with basin_radius; that 2D map is order-blind (shuffle the carve order and the point-cloud is byte-identical) — the same distribution-not-dynamics gap Lane M PR #1760 found. Extend the carve coord to [x,y,t] encoding the carve-step/curriculum index."
  claim     = "On a STANDALONE toy (N=64, 3 seeds, deterministic toy Psi placement, CPU $0), the [x,y,t] map captures carve-sequence: all 4 encodings are shuffle-SENSITIVE (per-concept t shift ~0.33 >> 0.252 noise band) while the 2D map is EXACTLY order-invariant (delta=0.000); the spatial [x,y] substructure is byte-preserved (max diff 0.0). Order-recovery beats the order-blind 2D baseline (chance, rho=-0.03) for the 3 monotone encodings (raw_index/sinusoidal/cumulative_order, rho=+1.000); the periodic phase_of_cycle is INCONCLUSIVE (rho=0.111 < noise, shuffle-sensitive but absolute order not recoverable)."
  falsifier = "Pre-registered: HOLD requires order-recovery |rho| > 2-sigma chance AND > 2D baseline by 2-sigma (F-ORDER), 2D order-invariant AND [x,y,t] shuffle-sensitive >2-sigma (F-SHUFFLE), and [x,y] byte-identical after appending t (F-SPATIAL-PRESERVE). phase_of_cycle FAILED F-ORDER (rho 0.111 < 0.252) -> recorded INCONCLUSIVE, not rounded to HOLD."
  target    = "3/4 encodings HOLDS (raw_index, sinusoidal, cumulative_order); phase_of_cycle INCONCLUSIVE. The shuffle control (2D delta=0.000 vs time delta>0) is the non-tautological beat-the-baseline evidence."
  scope     = "TOY: deterministic toy Psi placement, NOT the real conscious_decoder / 603MB s16 carve; CPU/$0; STANDALONE (no wiring into engine_tensionlink_bench / clm_time_encoding / lane_m_eeg_mitosis). scale-transfer UNVERIFIED (a_toy_scale_recheck, a_scale_honest_scope)."
  honest    = "For the monotone encodings t is a 1-1 function of carve-step, so the order-recovery rho=+1.000 is near-tautological at toy scale (decode reads back the encoding) — it proves recoverability but the perfect score is a toy artifact, not a hard inference. The honest, non-tautological evidence is the SHUFFLE control and the 2D-baseline chance contrast. No fabrication; verdicts verbatim (p7/g5)."
  note      = "harness UNIVERSE/kosmos_time_axis_toy.py; verdicts .verdicts/kosmos-time-axis/{F-ORDER,F-SHUFFLE,F-SPATIAL-PRESERVE,SUMMARY}.txt + results.json + run_stdout.txt. Resolves the static-2D order-blind gap of the s16 carving (a_paper_negative_ok: phase_of_cycle is a clean partial-null). Parallels Lane M distribution-not-dynamics (PR #1760)."
